{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Adjoint $[2,1,0]^2$, untwisted two-rotation family: $\\kappa_{\\rm singlet}(t)$ and $\\Delta_c(t,\\tau_c)$ from first-order perturbation theory (2026-10-10)\n\ngl(3) XXX, $L=2$, adjoint on both sites, new conventions (Lax $\\mathcal L_{ij}(u)=u\\delta_{ij}+hE_{ij}$, twist on the right), plain GT generators `JJ`, exact arithmetic, $h=1$, $\\theta=(t,0)$ with **$t$ symbolic**. Spec: `Adjoint-untwist-perturbative-spec.md`; the closed forms to derive are in `L2-210-untwist-CG.md` sections 1 and 4; the pattern (first-order PT of the eigenvector, $\\Psi=h+\\varepsilon\\psi_1$) is that of `Adjoint-clean-analytic.wb`.\n\n**Regime.** $z=1+\\varepsilon\\varphi$, $w_1=1+\\varepsilon\\omega_1$, $w_2=1+\\varepsilon\\omega_2$, $y=w_2y_0$, $y_0=(t-1)/(t-2)$. Covectors $v_2=e_1^T\\rho(n)$, $v_1=v_2\\rho(\\Delta)$, $\\Delta_k=1/(w_2-z_k)$. With $V_1:=v_1/\\delta^\\Lambda=v_2\\,\\rho({\\rm diag}(D_k))/(D_1^2D_2)$, $D_k=1/(\\omega_2-\\varphi_k)$, the only $\\varepsilon$-dependence is in $v_2$ (through the Gauss parameters $r_k(\\varepsilon)$).\n\n**Method.** A generic member $M=t_1(3/7)+\\tfrac53t_2(1/5)$ of the commuting family (a second member $t_1(2/9)-\\tfrac74t_2(-3/5)$ is used as a check), restricted to a weight sector. $M_1=\\partial_\\varepsilon M$ is exact because $t_a(u;z)=\\sum_{|I|=a}z_I\\,m_I(u)$ with the untwisted principal quantum minors $m_I$. $\\psi_1$ solves $(M_0-m_0)\\psi_1=-(M_1-m_1)h$, $\\ell\\cdot\\psi_1=0$ ($\\ell$ the left eigenvector; $M_0$ is gl(3)-invariant but not symmetric in the plain basis). Irrep decompositions use projectors built from $C_2+C_3/7$.\n\n**Parametrizing the octets.** The characteristic polynomial of $t_2(\\theta_1+h)$ on ${\\rm HW}_{(3,2,1)}$ has discriminant $9(5t^2+4)$, a conic in $(t,\\tau)$: $t=4m/(5-m^2)$, $\\sqrt{5t^2+4}=(10+2m^2)/(5-m^2)=2+mt$ makes both $\\tau_\\pm$ rational functions of the single symbol $m$. So every octet computation is **exact and symbolic** (no `RootReduce`, no sampling): an identity in $m$ is an identity on the whole curve $\\tau^2-b\\tau+c=0$, i.e. for both copies at all $t$. The deck involution is $m\\to-5/m$.\n\n**Evidence tags.** All results below are exact symbolic identities in $(t,\\varphi_1,\\varphi_2,\\varphi_3,\\omega_1,\\omega_2)$ (octets: in $(m,\\varphi,\\omega)$), except the finite-$\\varepsilon$ cross-check (80 digits, numerical).\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 0. Setup\nGenerators, invariant metric $G$, HW kets per weight sector; checks as in `L2-210-untwist-CG.wb` cell 3. The first code cell clears the (shared) kernel.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* fresh kernel state; Quiet because the front-end wrapper symbol ClearGlobals is Protected *)\nQuiet[ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]];\n(* GT basis and gl(3) generators, verbatim from the L2-210-untwist-CG.wb setup *)\nps[rep_] := ps[rep] = Block[{res = (Prepend[rep, #1] &) /@ Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]}, If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse[Sort[res]], Reverse[Sort[Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]]]];\ndim[rep_] := dim[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] := Jp[k][pat] = -Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJm[k_][pat_] := Jm[k][pat] = Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := JJ[k, l, rep] = Which[\n  k == l, DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]],\n  l == k + 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l == k - 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l > k + 1, JJ[k, k + 1, rep] . JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k + 1, rep],\n  l < k - 1, JJ[k, k - 1, rep] . JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k - 1, rep]];\nchecks = <||>;\nLam = {2, 1, 0}; nL = 2; d1 = dim[Lam]; d2 = d1^nL; id1 = IdentityMatrix[d1]; id2 = IdentityMatrix[d2, SparseArray];\nEe[i_, j_] := Ee[i, j] = JJ[i, j, Lam];\nE1[i_, j_] := E1[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[SparseArray[Ee[i, j]], IdentityMatrix[d1, SparseArray]];\nE2[i_, j_] := E2[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[d1, SparseArray], SparseArray[Ee[i, j]]];\nEtot[i_, j_] := Etot[i, j] = E1[i, j] + E2[i, j];\n(* total gl(3) weight of each product basis state, in KroneckerProduct order; one-site weights *)\nwtBasis = Flatten[Table[Table[J0[k][p1] + J0[k][p2], {k, 3}], {p1, ps[{Lam}]}, {p2, ps[{Lam}]}], 1];\nwt1 = Table[Table[J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Lam}]}];\nsecOf[mu_] := secOf[mu] = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, mu]];\nkron[a_, b_] := Flatten[KroneckerProduct[a, b]];\ne1 = UnitVector[d1, 1];\ncomm = Flatten[Table[Ee[i, j] . Ee[k, l] - Ee[k, l] . Ee[i, j] - (KroneckerDelta[j, k] Ee[i, l] - KroneckerDelta[l, i] Ee[k, j]), {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {k, 3}, {l, 3}]];\nchecks[\"JJ gl(3) relations\"] = Union[comm] === {0};\n(* invariant diagonal metric G (G[[1]] = 1): Ee[i,j]^T G = G Ee[j,i]; JJ is not Hermitian, so projectors that must be orthogonal are G-orthogonal *)\ngv = Array[gg, d1];\ngsol = Solve[Flatten[Append[Table[Transpose[Ee[i, j]] . DiagonalMatrix[gv] - DiagonalMatrix[gv] . Ee[j, i], {i, 3}, {j, i + 1, 3}], {gv[[1]] - 1}]] == 0, gv];\ngMet = DiagonalMatrix[gv /. First[gsol]];\nchecks[\"G unique, positive, invariant\"] = Length[gsol] === 1 && And @@ Positive[Diagonal[gMet]] && And @@ Flatten[Table[Transpose[Ee[i, j]] . gMet === gMet . Ee[j, i], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\ngd2 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[Diagonal[gMet], Diagonal[gMet]]];\n(* exp of nilpotent root generators (E^3 = 0), rho(diag) *)\nexpN[a_] := IdentityMatrix[Length[a]] + a + a . a/2 + a . a . a/6 + a . a . a . a/24;\nchecks[\"nilpotency Ee[i,j]^3 = 0 (i != j)\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[If[i == j, True, MatrixPower[Ee[i, j], 3] === 0 Ee[i, j]], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\nrhoDiag[d_] := DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[d[[k]]^J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Lam}]}]];\n(* HW kets of V(x)V: common null space of the total raising ops per weight sector *)\nraiseM = Join[Etot[1, 2], Etot[1, 3], Etot[2, 3]];\nhwSecs = {{4, 2, 0}, {4, 1, 1}, {3, 3, 0}, {3, 2, 1}, {2, 2, 2}};\nhwKets[mu_] := hwKets[mu] = Module[{sec = secOf[mu], ns}, ns = NullSpace[Normal[raiseM[[All, sec]]]]; Table[Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> v], {d2}]], {v, ns}]];\nchecks[\"HW multiplicities (420,411,330,321,222) = (1,1,1,2,1)\"] = Length[hwKets[#]] & /@ hwSecs;\nchecks[\"sector sizes (420,411,330,321,222)\"] = Length[secOf[#]] & /@ hwSecs;\nGrid[{{\"d1, d2\", {d1, d2}}, {\"checks\", ToString[Normal[checks]]}, {\"diag G\", ToString[Diagonal[gMet]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Two-site transfer matrices, h = 1, theta = (t, 0), t SYMBOLIC. Monodromy T(v) = L1(v - t) L2(v), Lax L_ij(u) = u delta_ij + E_ij (new convention, untwisted). Principal quantum minors m_I(u) = sum_sigma sgn(sigma) prod_k T[[sigma_k, I_k]](u-(k-1)); the twisted transfer matrix is t_a(u; z) = sum_{|I|=a} z_I m_I(u), z_I = prod_{i in I} z_i, so with z = 1 + eps phi: t_a(u; eps) = t_a0 + eps t_a' + O(eps^2), t_a' = sum_I (sum_{i in I} phi_i) m_I. Principal minors preserve the total weight, so everything is block-diagonal in the weight sectors. *)\nTm[v_] := Tm[v] = Table[Sum[(KroneckerDelta[i, k] (v - t) id2 + E1[i, k]) . (KroneckerDelta[k, j] v id2 + E2[k, j]), {k, 3}], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\n(* block of m_I(u) on the weight sector mu, exact in t *)\nmI[I_, u_, mu_] := mI[I, u, mu] = Module[{sec = secOf[mu]}, Expand[Normal[Sum[Signature[s] Dot @@ Table[If[k == 1, Tm[u - (k - 1)][[s[[k]], I[[k]]]][[sec]], If[k == Length[I], Tm[u - (k - 1)][[s[[k]], I[[k]]]][[All, sec]], Tm[u - (k - 1)][[s[[k]], I[[k]]]]]], {k, Length[I]}], {s, Permutations[I]}]]]];\nmIsingle[I_, u_, mu_] := If[Length[I] == 1, Expand[Normal[Tm[u][[I[[1]], I[[1]]]][[secOf[mu], secOf[mu]]]]], mI[I, u, mu]];\nt0Sec[a_, u_, mu_] := Sum[mIsingle[I, u, mu], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\n(* eps-derivative of t_a(u; z = 1 + eps phi), phi symbolic list ph *)\nt1Sec[a_, u_, mu_, ph_] := Sum[(Total[ph[[I]]]) mIsingle[I, u, mu], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\n(* checks on the (3,2,1) sector: quantum determinant is not needed here; commutativity of t_a0 and of the first order [t_a0(u), t_b'(v)] + [t_a'(u), t_b0(v)] = 0 *)\nphS = {p1, p2, p3};\nmuT = {3, 2, 1};\n{tcheck, cm0} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[Simplify[t0Sec[a, u0, muT] . t0Sec[b, v0, muT] - t0Sec[b, v0, muT] . t0Sec[a, u0, muT]], {a, 1, 2}, {b, 1, 2}, {u0, {3/7}}, {v0, {1/5}}]];\ncm1 = Table[Simplify[t0Sec[a, 3/7, muT] . t1Sec[b, 1/5, muT, phS] - t1Sec[b, 1/5, muT, phS] . t0Sec[a, 3/7, muT] + t1Sec[a, 3/7, muT, phS] . t0Sec[b, 1/5, muT] - t0Sec[b, 1/5, muT] . t1Sec[a, 3/7, muT, phS]], {a, 1, 2}, {b, 1, 2}];\nchecks[\"t_a(u) commute (sector (3,2,1), symbolic t)\"] = Union[Flatten[cm0]] === {0};\nchecks[\"first-order commutation [t_a0, t_b'] + [t_a', t_b0] = 0 (sector (3,2,1), symbolic t, phi)\"] = Union[Flatten[cm1]] === {0};\nGrid[{{\"time (s)\", tcheck}, {\"commute (zeroth order)\", checks[\"t_a(u) commute (sector (3,2,1), symbolic t)\"]}, {\"commute (first order)\", checks[\"first-order commutation [t_a0, t_b'] + [t_a', t_b0] = 0 (sector (3,2,1), symbolic t, phi)\"]}}, Frame -> All]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* The regime and the covectors, exact in (eps, t, phi, omega). z = 1 + eps phi, w1 = 1 + eps om1, w2 = 1 + eps om2, y = w2 y0, y0 = (theta12 - h)/(theta12 - 2h) = (t-1)/(t-2). One-site vacuum covector v2 = e1^T rho(n) with n = exp(r1 E12) exp(r2 E13) exp(r3 E23) (Gauss parameters of Omega_(w1, y) for the ket twist z); v1 = v2 rho(Delta), Delta_k = 1/(w2 - z_k). Since rho(Delta)_p = prod_k Delta_k^J0_k[p] and delta^Lambda = Delta_1^2 Delta_2, V1 := v1/delta^Lambda = v2 . rhoDiag(D)/(D1^2 D2) with D_k = 1/(om2 - phi_k): the only eps dependence is in v2. *)\ny0S = (t - 1)/(t - 2);\nzS = 1 + ep phS; w1S = 1 + ep om1; w2S = 1 + ep om2; yS = w2S y0S;\nrsOf[zz_, w1_, y_] := {(w1 - zz[[1]])/(w1 - zz[[2]]), ((w1 - zz[[1]]) (zz[[1]] - y) (zz[[2]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]]) (y - zz[[3]])), ((w1 - zz[[2]]) (zz[[2]] - y) (zz[[1]] - zz[[3]]))/((zz[[1]] - zz[[2]]) (w1 - zz[[3]]) (zz[[3]] - y))};\nrN[r_] := expN[r[[1]] Ee[1, 2]] . expN[r[[2]] Ee[1, 3]] . expN[r[[3]] Ee[2, 3]];\nrNinv[r_] := expN[-r[[3]] Ee[2, 3]] . expN[-r[[2]] Ee[1, 3]] . expN[-r[[1]] Ee[1, 2]];\nrv[ep_] := Together /@ rsOf[1 + ep phS, 1 + ep om1, (1 + ep om2) y0S];\nrvS = rv[ep];\nrv0 = Together /@ (rvS /. ep -> 0); rv1 = Together /@ (D[rvS, ep] /. ep -> 0);\nDv = Table[1/(om2 - phS[[k]]), {k, 3}];\nv2fun[r_] := e1 . rN[r];\nV1fun[r_] := v2fun[r] . rhoDiag[Dv]/(Dv[[1]]^2 Dv[[2]]);\nphitfun[r_] := V1fun[r] . rNinv[r];   (* phi(eps)/delta^Lambda, the undone covector *)\n(* zeroth and first order pieces of v2, V1, phit (polynomials in r: exact Taylor) *)\ntay[f_] := Module[{rr = rvS, F = f[rvS]}, {Together /@ (F /. ep -> 0), Together /@ (D[F, ep] /. ep -> 0)}];\n{v20, v21} = tay[v2fun]; {V10, V11} = tay[V1fun]; {pt0, pt1} = tay[phitfun];\n(* checks ---------------------------------------------------------------- *)\n(* (a) exact undo at a rational point: <V1(x)v2|HW> = <phit(x)e1|HW> for all 6 HW kets (rho(n)(x)rho(n) fixes HW) *)\nptTest = {t -> 5/2, p1 -> 1/3, p2 -> -2/7, p3 -> 5/11, om1 -> 3/4, om2 -> -1/5, ep -> 1/1000};\nhwAll = Join @@ (hwKets /@ hwSecs);\nchecks[\"undo exact: <V1 x v2|HW> = <phit x e1|HW>, 6 HW kets (rational point)\"] = With[{r = rvS /. ptTest}, With[{V1p = V1fun[rvS] /. ptTest, v2p = v2fun[rvS] /. ptTest, php = phitfun[rvS] /. ptTest}, And @@ (kron[V1p, v2p] . # === kron[php, e1] . # & /@ hwAll)]];\nchecks[\"rho(n) x rho(n) fixes the HW kets (rational point)\"] = With[{r = rvS /. ptTest, R = rN[rvS /. ptTest]}, And @@ (KroneckerProduct[R, R] . # === # & /@ hwAll)];\n(* (b) Task-0 closed forms of the eps = 0 covector: a'0, c'0 and phit(0) = e1^T exp(a'0 E12) exp(c'0 E23) *)\na0S = (om1 - p1) (p2 - p1)/((om1 - p2) (om2 - p2));\nc0S = ((om1 - p2) (p1 - p3)/((p1 - p2) (om1 - p3))) (p3 - p2)/(om2 - p3);\nchecks[\"phit(0) = e1^T exp(a'0 E12) exp(c'0 E23), symbolic in (t, phi, om)\"] = Simplify[pt0 - e1 . expN[a0S Ee[1, 2]] . expN[c0S Ee[2, 3]]] === ConstantArray[0, d1];\n(* n' = Delta^-1 n Delta n^-1: a' (eps-free), c', b' and b'/(a'c') = 1 + eps (t-2)(phi2 - om2) + O(eps^2) *)\nnMat[r_] := {{1, r[[1]], r[[2]] + r[[1]] r[[3]]}, {0, 1, r[[3]]}, {0, 0, 1}};\ndlM = DiagonalMatrix[Dv/ep];  (* Delta up to the common scalar convention: Delta = diag(1/(w2 - z_k)) = diag(Dv/ep) *)\nnprime = Together /@ (Inverse[dlM] . nMat[rvS] . dlM . Inverse[nMat[rvS]]);\napS = nprime[[1, 2]]; bpS = nprime[[1, 3]]; cpS = nprime[[2, 3]];\nchecks[\"a' is eps-free and = a'0 (symbolic)\"] = Simplify[apS - a0S] === 0;\nratSer = Series[Together[bpS/(apS cpS)], {ep, 0, 1}];\nchecks[\"b'/(a'c') = 1 + eps (t-2)(phi2 - om2) + O(eps^2) (symbolic)\"] = Simplify[SeriesCoefficient[ratSer, 0]] === 1 && Simplify[SeriesCoefficient[ratSer, 1] - (t - 2) (p2 - om2)] === 0;\nGrid[{{\"undo exact (6 HW kets)\", checks[\"undo exact: <V1 x v2|HW> = <phit x e1|HW>, 6 HW kets (rational point)\"]}, {\"R fixes HW\", checks[\"rho(n) x rho(n) fixes the HW kets (rational point)\"]}, {\"phit(0) = e1 exp(a'0 E12) exp(c'0 E23)\", checks[\"phit(0) = e1^T exp(a'0 E12) exp(c'0 E23), symbolic in (t, phi, om)\"]}, {\"a' eps-free\", checks[\"a' is eps-free and = a'0 (symbolic)\"]}, {\"b'/(a'c') first order\", checks[\"b'/(a'c') = 1 + eps (t-2)(phi2 - om2) + O(eps^2) (symbolic)\"]}}, Frame -> All]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. First-order perturbation theory machinery and irrep projectors\n`pert1` returns $m_0$, $\\ell$, and for each unit direction $i$ of $\\varphi$ the pair $(m_1,\\psi_1^{(i)})$ with residual checks; $\\psi_1=\\sum_i\\varphi_i\\psi_1^{(i)}$. `PiIrrep[mu, nu]` are the exact projectors onto the irreps in a weight sector.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* First-order perturbation theory of one eigenvector of the commuting family. A generic family member M(eps) = t1(u0; z) + rr t2(u1; z), z = 1 + eps phi, restricted to a weight sector: M = M0 + eps M1. M0 is gl(3)-invariant but NOT symmetric (plain JJ), so use the left eigenvector l:\n   (M0 - m0) psi1 = -(M1 - m1) h,  m1 = l.M1.h/(l.h),  l.psi1 = 0   (the component of psi1 along h is irrelevant)\n solved as the nonsingular system (M0 - m0 + h l/(l.h)) psi1 = -(M1 - m1) h  (apply l: l.psi1 = 0 follows since l.(M1 - m1).h = 0). Linear in phi: M1 = sum_i phi_i M1[i], so psi1 = sum_i phi_i psi1[i]. Entries are exact rational functions of t (or of the curve parameter m, cells below). *)\nfirstNZ[hv_] := Position[hv, _?(# =!= 0 &), {1}, 1, Heads -> False][[1, 1]];\nfamM0[mu_, u0_, u1_, rr_] := t0Sec[1, u0, mu] + rr t0Sec[2, u1, mu];\nfamM1[mu_, u0_, u1_, rr_, i_] := t1Sec[1, u0, mu, UnitVector[3, i]] + rr t1Sec[2, u1, mu, UnitVector[3, i]];\nsimp[x_] := Together[x];\npert1[M0_, M1s_, hv_, sub_ : {}] := Module[{n = Length[hv], A, k, m0, lv, P, out},\n  A = simp[M0 /. sub]; k = firstNZ[hv];\n  m0 = simp[(A . hv)[[k]]/hv[[k]]];\n  If[! (simp[(A - m0 IdentityMatrix[n]) . hv] === ConstantArray[0, n]), Return[$Failed]];\n  lv = simp[First[NullSpace[Transpose[A - m0 IdentityMatrix[n]]]]];\n  P = Outer[Times, hv, lv]/(lv . hv);\n  out = Table[Module[{B = simp[M1s[[i]] /. sub], m1, rhs, psi},\n     m1 = simp[lv . B . hv/(lv . hv)]; rhs = simp[-(B - m1 IdentityMatrix[n]) . hv];\n     psi = simp[LinearSolve[simp[A - m0 IdentityMatrix[n] + P], rhs]];\n     <|\"m1\" -> m1, \"psi1\" -> psi, \"res\" -> simp[(A - m0 IdentityMatrix[n]) . psi - rhs], \"lpsi\" -> simp[lv . psi]|>], {i, 3}];\n  <|\"m0\" -> m0, \"l\" -> lv, \"dir\" -> out|>];\n(* psi1 for a symbolic phi list *)\npsi1Of[res_, ph_] := Together[Sum[ph[[i]] res[\"dir\"][[i, \"psi1\"]], {i, 3}]];\n(* irrep projectors on a weight sector from the quadratic and cubic Casimirs: X = C2 + kap C3 (kap generic) has distinct values on the five irreps; Pi_nu = prod_{nu' != nu} (X - x_nu')/(x_nu - x_nu'). *)\nC2f = Sum[Etot[i, j] . Etot[j, i], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\nC3f = Sum[Etot[i, j] . Etot[j, k] . Etot[k, i], {i, 3}, {j, 3}, {k, 3}];\nkapX = 1/7; Xf = C2f + kapX C3f;\nirreps = {{4, 2, 0}, {4, 1, 1}, {3, 3, 0}, {3, 2, 1}, {2, 2, 2}};\nxVal = Association[Table[mu -> With[{hv = hwKets[mu][[1]]}, With[{w = Normal[Xf . hv]}, w[[firstNZ[hv]]]/hv[[firstNZ[hv]]]]], {mu, irreps}]];\nchecks[\"irrep invariants X = C2 + C3/7: all HW kets are eigenvectors; 5 distinct values\"] = {And @@ Flatten[Table[Normal[Xf . hk] == xVal[mu] hk, {mu, irreps}, {hk, hwKets[mu]}]], Length[Union[Values[xVal]]]};\nClearAll[xBlock, PiIrrep];\nxBlock[mu_] := xBlock[mu] = Normal[Xf[[secOf[mu], secOf[mu]]]];\nPiIrrep[mu_, nu_] := PiIrrep[mu, nu] = With[{X = xBlock[mu], n = Length[secOf[mu]]}, Module[{M = IdentityMatrix[n]}, Do[If[nu2 =!= nu, M = M . (X - xVal[nu2] IdentityMatrix[n])/(xVal[nu] - xVal[nu2])], {nu2, irreps}]; M]];\nchecks[\"Pi_nu on sectors (222, 321): idempotent, orthogonal, complete\"] = Table[With[{n = Length[secOf[mu]]}, {Total[PiIrrep[mu, #] & /@ irreps] === IdentityMatrix[n], And @@ Flatten[Table[PiIrrep[mu, a] . PiIrrep[mu, b] === If[a === b, PiIrrep[mu, a], 0 PiIrrep[mu, a]], {a, irreps}, {b, irreps}]], Table[MatrixRank[PiIrrep[mu, nu]], {nu, irreps}]}], {mu, {{2, 2, 2}, {3, 2, 1}}}];\nGrid[{{\"X invariants\", ToString[checks[\"irrep invariants X = C2 + C3/7: all HW kets are eigenvectors; 5 distinct values\"]]}, {\"Pi_nu: (complete, orthogonal, ranks per irrep 420,411,330,321,222) for sectors (2,2,2), (3,2,1)\", ToString[checks[\"Pi_nu on sectors (222, 321): idempotent, orthogonal, complete\"]]}}, Frame -> All]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. Singlet (Claim 1), sector $(2,2,2)$, $t,\\varphi,\\omega$ all symbolic",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* SINGLET (Claim 1), sector (2,2,2) (dim 10), t symbolic. Family member M = t1(3/7) + (5/3) t2(1/5). *)\nmuS = {2, 2, 2}; secS = secOf[muS]; hSfull = hwKets[muS][[1]]; hS = hSfull[[secS]];\nchecks[\"singlet ket is gl(3)-invariant (annihilated by all 6 E_ij, i != j, and E_ii - 2)\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[Normal[Etot[i, j] . hSfull] == If[i == j, 2 hSfull, 0 hSfull], {i, 3}, {j, 3}]];\n{tPS, resS} = AbsoluteTiming[pert1[famM0[muS, 3/7, 1/5, 5/3], Table[famM1[muS, 3/7, 1/5, 5/3, i], {i, 3}], hS]];\npsiS = psi1Of[resS, phS];\nchecks[\"singlet: h is an eigenvector of M0, eigenvalue m0 (symbolic t)\"] = resS =!= $Failed;\nchecks[\"singlet: psi1 equation residual (M0 - m0) psi1 + (M1 - m1) h = 0 and l.psi1 = 0 (3 directions)\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[{resS[\"dir\"][[i, \"res\"]] === ConstantArray[0, 10], resS[\"dir\"][[i, \"lpsi\"]] === 0}, {i, 3}]];\n(* covectors restricted to the sector *)\ncov0S = kron[V10, v20][[secS]];\ncov1S = (kron[V11, v20] + kron[V10, v21])[[secS]];\ns0S = Simplify[cov0S . hS]; s1S = Simplify[cov1S . hS];\n(* undone form of the signal: <phit(eps) (x) e1|h>, same thing *)\ns1Und = Simplify[(kron[pt1, e1][[secS]]) . hS];\n(* closed form of the claim *)\nidx012 = Position[wt1, {0, 1, 2}][[1, 1]];\nCsS = hSfull[[(idx012 - 1) d1 + 1]];\nS1claim = -3 (t - 2) (p2 - om2) (a0S c0S)^2 CsS;\nK1S = Simplify[cov0S . psiS];\nGrid[{{\"time (s) for psi1 (3 directions, symbolic t)\", tPS}, {\"m0(t)\", Factor[resS[\"m0\"]]}, {\"<V1 x v2|h> at eps^0 (must be 0)\", s0S}, {\"S1 = d/deps <V1 x v2|h>\", Factor[s1S]}, {\"S1 from the undone covector phit(eps) (x) e1\", Simplify[s1S - s1Und]}, {\"S1 - closed form -3(t-2)(phi2-om2)(a'0 c'0)^2 C_singlet\", Simplify[s1S - S1claim]}, {\"C_singlet = h[(0,1,2) (x) e1]\", CsS}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Claim 1: K1/S1, independence of the family member, and the per-irrep decomposition of K1 (which intermediate irreps carry the contamination). *)\nratioS = Simplify[K1S/s1S];\nchecks[\"Claim 1: K1/S1 = -t/(3(t-2)) exactly, symbolic in (t, phi, om1, om2)\"] = Simplify[ratioS + t/(3 (t - 2))] === 0;\n(* a second, different generic family member: M' = t1(2/9) - (7/4) t2(-3/5) *)\nresS2 = pert1[famM0[muS, 2/9, -3/5, -7/4], Table[famM1[muS, 2/9, -3/5, -7/4, i], {i, 3}], hS];\npsiS2 = psi1Of[resS2, phS];\nK1S2 = Simplify[cov0S . psiS2];\nchecks[\"Claim 1: K1 independent of the family member (symbolic): K1 - K1' = 0, and psi1 - psi1' is parallel to h\"] = {Simplify[K1S - K1S2] === 0, Simplify[(psiS - psiS2) - hS ((psiS - psiS2)[[firstNZ[hS]]]/hS[[firstNZ[hS]]])] === ConstantArray[0, 10]};\n(* per-irrep decomposition K1 = sum_nu <cov|Pi_nu psi1>; octet pair summed; the singlet component of psi1 vanishes by l.psi1 = 0 *)\nK1nu = Association[Table[nu -> Simplify[cov0S . (PiIrrep[muS, nu] . psiS)], {nu, irreps}]];\nfracNu = Association[Table[nu -> Factor[K1nu[nu]/s1S], {nu, irreps}]];\nchecks[\"Claim 1: sum over irreps of K1_nu/S1 = -t/(3(t-2))\"] = Simplify[Total[Values[fracNu]] + t/(3 (t - 2))] === 0;\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{StringJoin[\"[\", Riffle[ToString /@ nu, \",\"], \"]\"], Switch[nu, {4, 2, 0}, \"27\", {4, 1, 1}, \"10\", {3, 3, 0}, \"10bar\", {3, 2, 1}, \"8 + 8 (both copies)\", {2, 2, 2}, \"1 (h itself)\"], fracNu[nu], Apart[fracNu[nu], t]}, {nu, irreps}], {\"irrep nu of |n>\", \"dim\", \"K1_nu/S1\", \"partial fractions in t\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Octets (Claim 2), sector $(3,2,1)$\nFirst $\\tau_c$, then $\\psi_1$ and the top-killed overlap, written as $g_c=F_1/F_0=[\\langle\\partial_\\varepsilon(V_1\\otimes v_2-v_2\\otimes v_2)|h_c\\rangle+\\langle V_1^0\\otimes v_2^0-v_2^0\\otimes v_2^0|\\psi_1\\rangle]/{\\rm Sig}_0$, with ${\\rm Sig}_0=\\langle V_1^0\\otimes v_2^0|h_c\\rangle=a'_0c'_0\\,(u+u')\\cdot C_c$ (the factors $\\delta^\\Lambda$, $a'_0c'_0$ and the scalar normalization series cancel in $F_1/F_0$ up to an $\\omega_2$-independent constant).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* OCTETS, step 1: the two octet HW kets are the eigenvectors of t2(theta1 + h) on HW_(3,2,1) (2-dim). Restrict the operator (sector block) to the HW kets: M.H = H.A with H the 6x2 matrix of HW kets; tau_c are the eigenvalues of the 2x2 matrix A(t), exact in t. *)\nsecO = secOf[{3, 2, 1}]; muO = {3, 2, 1};\nHO = Transpose[hwKets[muO][[All, secO]]];   (* 6 x 2 *)\nMtau = t0Sec[2, t + 1, muO];\nAO = Together[PseudoInverse[HO] . Mtau . HO];\nchecks[\"t2(theta1+h) H = H A (HW space invariant), symbolic t\"] = Simplify[Mtau . HO - HO . AO] === ConstantArray[0, {6, 2}];\ncpoly = Factor[CharacteristicPolynomial[AO, tau]];\ntauCharClaim = tau^2 - 3 (2 t - 1) (t + 2) tau + 9 t (t - 1) (t + 1) (t + 3);\nchecks[\"char poly of t2(theta1+h) on HW_(3,2,1) = tau^2 - 3(2t-1)(t+2) tau + 9t(t-1)(t+1)(t+3)\"] = Simplify[cpoly - tauCharClaim] === 0;\n(* the discriminant is 9(5t^2+4): the curve {tau^2 - b tau + c = 0} is a conic cover of the t-line, rational with parameter m: t = 4m/(5 - m^2), s := sqrt(5t^2+4) = (10+2m^2)/(5-m^2) = 2 + m t. Then tau_pm = (3(2t-1)(t+2) +- 3 s)/2 are RATIONAL functions of m, and every identity in m is an exact identity on the whole curve (both copies). *)\ntOfm = 4 m/(5 - m^2); sOfm = (10 + 2 m^2)/(5 - m^2);\nchecks[\"s^2 = 5t^2 + 4 and s = 2 + m t on the parametrization\"] = {Simplify[sOfm^2 - (5 tOfm^2 + 4)] === 0, Simplify[sOfm - (2 + m tOfm)] === 0};\ntauPm[sg_] := Together[(3 (2 tOfm - 1) (tOfm + 2) + sg 3 sOfm)/2];\nchecks[\"tau_pm(m) solve the quadratic identically in m\"] = Table[Simplify[(tauCharClaim /. {t -> tOfm, tau -> tauPm[sg]})] === 0, {sg, {1, -1}}];\n(* eigenvector of A for tau: c = (A12, tau - A11); second row of (A - tau) c = 0 holds on the curve *)\nhcOf[sg_] := Together[HO . ({AO[[1, 2]], tau - AO[[1, 1]]} /. tau -> tauPm[sg]) /. t -> tOfm];\nchecks[\"h_c(m) is a common HW eigenvector: t2(theta1+h) h_c = tau_c h_c and E_raise h_c = 0 (both copies, symbolic m)\"] = Table[With[{hv = hcOf[sg]}, {Simplify[(Mtau /. t -> tOfm) . hv - tauPm[sg] hv] === ConstantArray[0, 6], Simplify[Normal[raiseM[[All, secO]]] . hv] === ConstantArray[0, 3 d2]}], {sg, {1, -1}}];\nGrid[{{\"A(t) = t2(theta1+h) on HW_(3,2,1)\", MatrixForm[Factor[AO]]}, {\"char poly (derived)\", cpoly}, {\"= claimed\", Simplify[cpoly - tauCharClaim] === 0}, {\"tau_1 + tau_2 = Tr A\", Factor[Tr[AO]]}, {\"tau_1 tau_2 = Det A\", Factor[Det[AO]]}, {\"checks\", ToString[Normal[checks][[-6 ;; -1, 2]]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* OCTETS, step 2: psi1 of both octet copies (symbolic in the curve parameter m, hence in t and tau_c; phi symbolic), and the top-killed overlap Ftot = d/deps <(V1 x v2) - (v2 x v2) | h + eps psi1> normalized by the zeroth order Sig0 = <V1 x v2|h>:\n   g_c := F1/F0 = [ <d(V1 x v2 - v2 x v2)|h> + <V1^0 x v2^0 - v2^0 x v2^0|psi1> ] / Sig0 .\n (the common factors delta^Lambda, a'0 c'0 and the scalar normalization series cancel or are omega2-independent). *)\nidx111 = Flatten[Position[wt1, {1, 1, 1}]];\nuV = (e1 . Ee[1, 3])[[idx111]]; upV = (e1 . Ee[2, 3] . Ee[1, 2])[[idx111]];\nchecks[\"u = e1^T E13 and u' = e1^T E23 E12 live on the two (1,1,1) states, u + u' = (1,3)\"] = {uV, upV, uV + upV === {1, 3}, Total[Abs[e1 . Ee[1, 3]]] == Total[Abs[uV]], Total[Abs[e1 . Ee[2, 3] . Ee[1, 2]]] == Total[Abs[upV]]};\nfamU0 = 3/7; famU1 = 1/5; famR = 5/3;\n(* covectors carry t through y0 = (t-1)/(t-2): substitute the curve parametrization t = 4m/(5-m^2) *)\ncov0O = Together[kron[V10, v20][[secO]] /. t -> tOfm]; top0O = Together[kron[v20, v20][[secO]] /. t -> tOfm];\ndcovO = Together[(kron[V11, v20] + kron[V10, v21] - kron[v21, v20] - kron[v20, v21])[[secO]] /. t -> tOfm];   (* eps-derivative of the top-killed covector *)\nfullFromO[v_] := Normal[SparseArray[Thread[secO -> v], {d2}]];\noctet[sg_] := Module[{hv = hcOf[sg], res, psi, hFull, C, Rc, Sig0, dT, cT, tp = tauPm[sg], r},\n  res = pert1[famM0[muO, famU0, famU1, famR], Table[famM1[muO, famU0, famU1, famR, i], {i, 3}], hv, {t -> tOfm}];\n  psi = psi1Of[res, phS];\n  hFull = fullFromO[hv]; C = hFull[[(idx111 - 1) d1 + 1]]; Rc = Together[(uV . C)/((uV + upV) . C)];\n  Sig0 = Together[cov0O . hv]; dT = Together[dcovO . hv]; cT = Together[(cov0O - top0O) . psi];\n  <|\"sg\" -> sg, \"tau\" -> tp, \"hv\" -> hv, \"res\" -> res, \"psi\" -> psi, \"C\" -> C, \"R\" -> Rc, \"Sig0\" -> Sig0, \"dT\" -> dT, \"cT\" -> cT|>];\n{tOct, octs} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[octet[sg], {sg, {1, -1}}]];\nchecks[\"octet psi1: equation residual and l.psi1 = 0 (both copies, 3 directions, symbolic m)\"] = Table[And @@ Flatten[Table[{o[\"res\"][\"dir\"][[i, \"res\"]] === ConstantArray[0, 6], o[\"res\"][\"dir\"][[i, \"lpsi\"]] === 0}, {i, 3}]], {o, octs}];\n(* zeroth order: <V1 x v2|h> = a'0 c'0 (u + u').C and <v2 x v2|h> = 0 *)\nchecks[\"octet zeroth order: Sig0 = a'0 c'0 (u+u').C_c and <v2 x v2|h_c> = 0\"] = Table[{Simplify[o[\"Sig0\"] - ((a0S c0S) /. t -> tOfm) ((uV + upV) . o[\"C\"])] === 0, Simplify[top0O . o[\"hv\"]] === 0}, {o, octs}];\nGrid[{{\"time (s)\", tOct}, {\"checks\", ToString[Normal[checks][[-3 ;; -1, 2]]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Claim 2: g_c = F1/F0 is affine in om2 (exact), its slope is -(t-2) R_c + Delta_c with Delta_c = (1 - t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)); everything symbolic in (m, phi, om1, om2). *)\nDeltaClaim[tv_, tp_] := (1 - tv^2) + tv tp/(3 (tv + 3));\nanalyseOct[o_] := Module[{g, gs, gc, sl, Dl, aff, tv = tOfm, tp = o[\"tau\"]},\n  gs = Together[o[\"dT\"]/o[\"Sig0\"]]; gc = Together[o[\"cT\"]/o[\"Sig0\"]]; g = gs + gc;\n  aff = Simplify[D[g, {om2, 2}]];\n  sl = Simplify[D[g, om2]];\n  Dl = Simplify[sl + (tv - 2) o[\"R\"]];\n  <|\"g\" -> g, \"aff\" -> aff, \"slope\" -> sl, \"Delta\" -> Dl, \"Dsig\" -> Simplify[D[gs, om2] + (tv - 2) o[\"R\"]], \"Dcont\" -> Simplify[D[gc, om2]], \"om1dep\" -> Simplify[D[sl, om1]], \"phidep\" -> Simplify[D[sl, p1]] === 0 && Simplify[D[sl, p2]] === 0 && Simplify[D[sl, p3]] === 0, \"claim\" -> Simplify[Dl - DeltaClaim[tv, tp]]|>];\n{tAn, anO} = AbsoluteTiming[analyseOct /@ octs];\nchecks[\"Claim 2: g_c affine in om2 (d^2 g/d om2^2 = 0), symbolic\"] = (#[\"aff\"] === 0 & /@ anO);\nchecks[\"Claim 2: slope independent of om1 and of phi, symbolic\"] = {#[\"om1dep\"] === 0 & /@ anO, #[\"phidep\"] & /@ anO};\nchecks[\"Claim 2: Delta_c = slope + (t-2) R_c = (1 - t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)), both copies, symbolic in m\"] = (#[\"claim\"] === 0 & /@ anO);\nGrid[{{\"time (s)\", tAn}, {\"affine in om2\", checks[\"Claim 2: g_c affine in om2 (d^2 g/d om2^2 = 0), symbolic\"]}, {\"slope indep. of om1, phi\", ToString[checks[\"Claim 2: slope independent of om1 and of phi, symbolic\"]]}, {\"Delta_c - claim = 0 (copies +, -)\", checks[\"Claim 2: Delta_c = slope + (t-2) R_c = (1 - t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)), both copies, symbolic in m\"]}, {\"Delta_pm numerically at m = 1/3 (t = 3/11)\", N[Table[a[\"Delta\"] /. m -> 1/3, {a, anO}]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Octets: which intermediate irreps carry the contamination slope Delta_c? psi1 = sum_nu Pi_nu psi1 (Pi_nu commute with M0). Each piece contributes Delta_c^(nu) = d/d om2 [ <V1^0 x v2^0 - v2^0 x v2^0 | Pi_nu psi1> / Sig0 ]; sum over nu = Delta_c. Written as A_nu(t) + B_nu(t) tau_c by solving with the two copies (rational in t after the deck transformation m -> -5/m). *)\ntoT[f_] := Factor[Simplify[f /. m -> (Sqrt[5 t^2 + 4] - 2)/t]];\nDeltaNu[o_, nu_] := Simplify[D[Together[((cov0O - top0O) . (PiIrrep[muO, nu] . o[\"psi\"]))/o[\"Sig0\"]], om2]];\nDnuTab = Association[Table[nu -> Table[DeltaNu[o, nu], {o, octs}], {nu, irreps[[1 ;; 4]]}]];\nABof[x_] := Module[{B = Together[(x[[1]] - x[[2]])/(octs[[1]][\"tau\"] - octs[[2]][\"tau\"])]}, {toT[Together[x[[1]] - B octs[[1]][\"tau\"]]], toT[B]}];\nchecks[\"Claim 2 per irrep: sum_nu Delta_c^(nu) = Delta_c (both copies)\"] = Simplify[Total[Values[DnuTab]] - (anO[[All, \"Dcont\"]])] === {0, 0};\nABnu = Association[Table[nu -> ABof[DnuTab[nu]], {nu, irreps[[1 ;; 4]]}]];\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{StringJoin[\"[\", Riffle[ToString /@ nu, \",\"], \"]\"], Switch[nu, {4, 2, 0}, \"27\", {4, 1, 1}, \"10\", {3, 3, 0}, \"10bar\", {3, 2, 1}, \"8 (the other copy)\"], ABnu[nu][[1]], ABnu[nu][[2]]}, {nu, irreps[[1 ;; 4]]}], {\"irrep of |n>\", \"dim\", \"A_nu(t)  [ Delta^(nu) = A + B tau_c ]\", \"B_nu(t)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Singlet: the octet pair is the whole contamination (previous cell). Split it into the two octet copies with the spectral projectors of M0 inside the octet subspace of the (2,2,2) sector: Pi_c = Pi_8 (M0 - m0_c')/(m0_c - m0_c'), m0_c = eigenvalue of M0 (same family member as the singlet) on the octet HW ket of copy c (from the (3,2,1) computation). Each copy's share K1_c/S1 is algebraic in t, = A(t) + B(t) tau_c; the sum is -t/(3(t-2)). *)\nM0Sm = Together[famM0[muS, 3/7, 1/5, 5/3] /. t -> tOfm];\npsiSm = Together[psiS /. t -> tOfm]; cov0Sm = Together[cov0S /. t -> tOfm]; s1Sm = Together[s1S /. t -> tOfm];\nm0c = octs[[All, \"res\"]][[All, \"m0\"]];\nchecks[\"octet eigenvalues of M0 (sector (3,2,1)) are distinct and M0 Pi_8 has only these two eigenvalues on the (2,2,2) sector\"] = {Simplify[m0c[[1]] - m0c[[2]]] =!= 0, Simplify[(M0Sm - m0c[[1]] IdentityMatrix[10]) . (M0Sm - m0c[[2]] IdentityMatrix[10]) . PiIrrep[muS, {3, 2, 1}]] === ConstantArray[0, {10, 10}]};\nPiCopy[c_] := Together[PiIrrep[muS, {3, 2, 1}] . (M0Sm - m0c[[3 - c]] IdentityMatrix[10])/(m0c[[c]] - m0c[[3 - c]])];\nchecks[\"Pi_c: idempotent, Pi_1 + Pi_2 = Pi_8, M0 Pi_c = m0_c Pi_c\"] = {Simplify[PiCopy[1] . PiCopy[1] - PiCopy[1]] === ConstantArray[0, {10, 10}], Simplify[PiCopy[1] + PiCopy[2] - PiIrrep[muS, {3, 2, 1}]] === ConstantArray[0, {10, 10}], Simplify[M0Sm . PiCopy[1] - m0c[[1]] PiCopy[1]] === ConstantArray[0, {10, 10}]};\nK1c = Table[Simplify[cov0Sm . (PiCopy[c] . psiSm)/s1Sm], {c, 2}];\nABK = With[{B = Together[(K1c[[1]] - K1c[[2]])/(octs[[1]][\"tau\"] - octs[[2]][\"tau\"])]}, {toT[Together[K1c[[1]] - B octs[[1]][\"tau\"]]], toT[B]}];\nchecks[\"singlet: K1_1/S1 + K1_2/S1 = -t/(3(t-2)) (symbolic in m)\"] = Simplify[Total[K1c] + tOfm/(3 (tOfm - 2))] === 0;\nchecks[\"singlet: K1_c/S1 = A(t) + B(t) tau_c with A, B rational in t\"] = ABK;\nGrid[{{\"checks\", ToString[Normal[checks][[-3 ;; -1, 2]]]}, {\"K1_c/S1 = A + B tau_c: A(t)\", ABK[[1]]}, {\"B(t)\", ABK[[2]]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. Bonus: the clean branches $[4,1,1]$ and $[3,3,0]$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* BONUS: the clean branches [4,1,1] and [3,3,0] (sectors of dimension 2: the 10 / 10bar HW ket and the 27 descendant). S0 = <V1^0 x v2^0|h> (leading signal), K1 = <V1^0 x v2^0|psi1> (O(eps) contamination relative to S0 after multiplying by eps); also the top-killed version, where the vacuum overlap <v2 x v2|.> is subtracted. Exact in (t, phi, om1, om2). *)\ncleanBranch[mu_] := Module[{sec = secOf[mu], hf = hwKets[mu][[1]], hv, res, psi, cov, top, S0, K1, K1tk},\n  hv = hf[[sec]];\n  res = pert1[famM0[mu, 3/7, 1/5, 5/3], Table[famM1[mu, 3/7, 1/5, 5/3, i], {i, 3}], hv];\n  psi = psi1Of[res, phS];\n  cov = kron[V10, v20][[sec]]; top = kron[v20, v20][[sec]];\n  S0 = Simplify[cov . hv]; K1 = Simplify[cov . psi]; K1tk = Simplify[(cov - top) . psi];\n  <|\"mu\" -> mu, \"S0\" -> S0, \"K1\" -> K1, \"ratio\" -> Simplify[K1/S0], \"ratioTK\" -> Simplify[K1tk/S0], \"top0\" -> Simplify[top . hv], \"psi\" -> psi, \"hv\" -> hv|>];\ncleans = cleanBranch /@ {{4, 1, 1}, {3, 3, 0}};\nGrid[Prepend[Table[{c[\"mu\"], Factor[c[\"S0\"]], Factor[c[\"ratio\"]], Factor[c[\"ratioTK\"]]}, {c, cleans}], {\"branch\", \"S0 = <V1^0 x v2^0|h>\", \"K1/S0 (plain)\", \"K1^tk/S0 (top-killed)\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Cross-checks: independent finite-$\\varepsilon$ evaluation, second family member, $P_1$",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* INDEPENDENT FINITE-EPS CHECK of the octet result at the rational point m = 2 (t = 8, where tau_pm = 252, 198 are rational). No Taylor pieces and no m-symbolics: build the exactly twisted sector operator M(eps) = sum_I z_I [m_I(3/7) + (5/3) m_I(1/5)] at eps = 10^-8 (80 digits), take its true eigenvector near h_c, and the exact finite-eps covectors from rsOf. Tests (i) psi1 = (Psi - h)/eps (l.Psi = l.h) and (ii) the top-killed overlap ratio F(eps)/Sig0 = 1 + eps g, g affine in om2 with slope -(t-2)R_c + Delta_c. *)\nmFix = 2; tFix = tOfm /. m -> mFix;\nphFix = {1/3, -2/7, 5/11}; o1Fix = 3/4; epFix = 10^-8; precFix = 80;\nsubFix = Join[{t -> tFix, m -> mFix}, Thread[phS -> phFix], {om1 -> o1Fix}];\nMfull[epv_] := N[(Sum[(1 + epv phFix[[I[[1]]]]) mIsingle[I, 3/7, muO], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {1}]}] + 5/3 Sum[(Times @@ (1 + epv phFix[[I]])) mIsingle[I, 1/5, muO], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {2}]}]) /. t -> tFix, precFix];\nfiniteTest[sg_, om2v_] := Module[{o = octs[[If[sg == 1, 1, 2]]], hv, lv, M, es, k, Psi, psiNum, psiEx, rr, v2f, V1f, ovl, Sig0, gNum, pe, hvN, lvN, M0N},\n  hv = o[\"hv\"] /. m -> mFix; lv = o[\"res\"][\"l\"] /. m -> mFix;\n  M = Mfull[epFix]; M0N = N[(famM0[muO, 3/7, 1/5, 5/3] /. t -> tFix), precFix];\n  es = Eigensystem[M]; k = First@Ordering[Abs[es[[1]] - N[o[\"res\"][\"m0\"] /. m -> mFix, precFix]], 1];\n  Psi = es[[2, k]]; Psi = Psi (N[lv . hv, precFix]/(N[lv, precFix] . Psi));\n  psiNum = (Psi - N[hv, precFix])/epFix; psiEx = N[o[\"psi\"] /. subFix, precFix];\n  rr = N[rvS /. Join[subFix, {ep -> epFix, om2 -> om2v}], precFix];\n  v2f = e1 . rN[rr]; V1f = v2f . rhoDiag[Dv /. Join[subFix, {om2 -> om2v}]]/((Dv[[1]]^2 Dv[[2]]) /. Join[subFix, {om2 -> om2v}]);\n  ovl = ((kron[V1f, v2f] - kron[v2f, v2f])[[secO]]) . Psi;\n  Sig0 = N[(cov0O /. Join[subFix, {om2 -> om2v}]) . hv, precFix];\n  <|\"psiErr\" -> Norm[psiNum - psiEx]/Norm[psiEx], \"g\" -> (ovl/Sig0 - 1)/epFix|>];\nfin = Table[Table[finiteTest[sg, om2v], {om2v, {-1/5, 9/7, 5/3}}], {sg, {1, -1}}];\nslopeNum = Table[{(fin[[c, 2, \"g\"]] - fin[[c, 1, \"g\"]])/(9/7 + 1/5), (fin[[c, 3, \"g\"]] - fin[[c, 2, \"g\"]])/(5/3 - 9/7)}, {c, 2}];\nslopeEx = Table[(anO[[c]][\"slope\"] /. m -> mFix), {c, 2}];\nchecks[\"finite eps = 1e-8, t = 8: |psi1_numeric - psi1_exact|/|psi1| for both copies, 3 om2 (O(eps))\"] = Table[N[f[\"psiErr\"], 3], {c, 2}, {f, fin[[c]]}];\nchecks[\"finite eps: numeric slopes of g in om2 (two intervals) vs exact slope, both copies\"] = {N[slopeNum, 12], N[slopeEx, 12]};\nchecks[\"finite eps: Delta_c = slope + (t-2) R_c vs (1-t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)) at t = 8\"] = Table[{N[slopeNum[[c, 1]] + (tFix - 2) (octs[[c]][\"R\"] /. m -> mFix), 12], N[DeltaClaim[tFix, octs[[c]][\"tau\"] /. m -> mFix], 12]}, {c, 2}];\nGrid[{{\"t, tau_+, tau_-\", {tFix, octs[[1]][\"tau\"] /. m -> mFix, octs[[2]][\"tau\"] /. m -> mFix}}, {\"psi1 relative error (copy +, 3 om2; copy -, 3 om2)\", checks[\"finite eps = 1e-8, t = 8: |psi1_numeric - psi1_exact|/|psi1| for both copies, 3 om2 (O(eps))\"]}, {\"slopes: numeric (2 intervals) vs exact\", checks[\"finite eps: numeric slopes of g in om2 (two intervals) vs exact slope, both copies\"]}, {\"Delta_c from the finite-eps slope vs claim\", checks[\"finite eps: Delta_c = slope + (t-2) R_c vs (1-t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)) at t = 8\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Octet checks: (a) independence of the family member (M' = t1(2/9) - (7/4) t2(-3/5)); (b) whether the 27 and the other octet contribute at all to the top-killed overlap (not only to the omega2-slope); (c) the P1 value t = 62/35 against the earlier numerical Richardson/fit values of Delta_c (L2-210-untwist-CG.md section 4: Delta_1 = -1.1814355, Delta_2 = 0.4659522). *)\nBlock[{famU0 = 2/9, famU1 = -3/5, famR = -7/4}, octs2 = Table[octet[sg], {sg, {1, -1}}]];\nanO2 = analyseOct /@ octs2;\nchecks[\"octets, 2nd family member: Delta_c = (1-t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)) again (symbolic), and Delta_c(member 1) - Delta_c(member 2) = 0\"] = {#[\"claim\"] === 0 & /@ anO2, Simplify[anO2[[All, \"Delta\"]] - anO[[All, \"Delta\"]]] === {0, 0}, #[\"aff\"] === 0 & /@ anO2};\n(* not just the slope: the full contributions of each irrep to the top-killed contamination <V1^0 x v2^0 - v2^0 x v2^0|Pi_nu psi1> *)\ncontNu = Table[Simplify[(cov0O - top0O) . (PiIrrep[muO, nu] . octs[[c]][\"psi\"])] === 0, {c, 2}, {nu, irreps[[1 ;; 4]]}];\nchecks[\"octets: is <cov - top | Pi_nu psi1> identically 0? (False = nonzero), nu = 27, 10, 10bar, other octet; rows copy +, -\"] = contNu;\nt62 = 62/35; sq62 = Sqrt[5 t62^2 + 4];\ntau62 = {(3 (2 t62 - 1) (t62 + 2) + 3 sq62)/2, (3 (2 t62 - 1) (t62 + 2) - 3 sq62)/2};\nchecks[\"P1 t = 62/35: Delta_c from the closed form (tau_+, tau_-)\"] = N[DeltaClaim[t62, #] & /@ tau62, 10];\nGrid[{{\"2nd family member: claim holds (copies), members agree, affine\", ToString[checks[\"octets, 2nd family member: Delta_c = (1-t^2) + t tau_c/(3(t+3)) again (symbolic), and Delta_c(member 1) - Delta_c(member 2) = 0\"]]}, {\"is <cov-top|Pi_nu psi1> identically 0? (False = nonzero; nu = 27, 10, 10bar, octet; rows copy +, -). All four are nonzero, but only 10 and 10bar have an omega2-dependence\", ToString[contNu]}, {\"P1 (t = 62/35): Delta_{tau_+}, Delta_{tau_-} from the closed form\", checks[\"P1 t = 62/35: Delta_c from the closed form (tau_+, tau_-)\"]}, {\"earlier numerics at P1\", \"Delta_1 in [-1.18143555,-1.18143546], Delta_2 in [0.46595216,0.46595223]\"}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]\n",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Results (2026-10-10)\n\n**Execution note.** The file `Adjoint-untwist-perturbative.wb` was created from the cell sources by script (no create-notebook tool); each cell's source was run in the shared kernel K1 (VS Code did not execute cells of this file), so the cells carry no stored outputs. Every number below was obtained in the kernel; a full run takes a few seconds.\n\n**Setup checks.** gl(3) relations, invariant positive $G$ = diag(1,1,1,2,6,9,4,9), HW multiplicities (1,1,1,2,1), sector sizes (1,2,2,6,10); $[t_a(u),t_b(v)]=0$ and the first-order identity $[t_{a0},t_b']+[t_a',t_{b0}]=0$ (symbolic $t,\\varphi$); exact undo $\\langle V_1\\otimes v_2|HW\\rangle=\\langle\\tilde\\varphi\\otimes e_1|HW\\rangle$ and $\\rho(n)\\otimes\\rho(n)\\,HW=HW$ at a rational point; $\\tilde\\varphi(0)=e_1^Te^{a_0'E_{12}}e^{c_0'E_{23}}$, $a'$ $\\varepsilon$-free, $b'/(a'c')=1+\\varepsilon(t-2)(\\varphi_2-\\omega_2)+O(\\varepsilon^2)$ (all symbolic in $t,\\varphi,\\omega$).\n\n**Claim 1 (singlet): proved symbolically.** $S_1=\\frac{3(t-2)(\\omega_1-\\varphi_1)^2(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_3)^2(\\varphi_2-\\varphi_3)^2}{(\\omega_2-\\varphi_2)(\\omega_1-\\varphi_3)^2(\\omega_2-\\varphi_3)^2}$ equals $-3(t-2)(\\varphi_2-\\omega_2)(a_0'c_0')^2C_{\\rm singlet}$ ($C_{\\rm singlet}=1$ in the normalization used), and\n$$K_1/S_1=-\\frac{t}{3(t-2)}\\quad\\text{exactly, independent of }\\varphi,\\omega_1,\\omega_2,$$\nhence $\\kappa_{\\rm singlet}=1+K/S=2(t-3)/(3(t-2))$ ($=43/12$ at $t=62/35$). Independent of the family member (second member: $K_1-K_1'=0$ and $\\psi_1-\\psi_1'\\parallel h$).\n\n*Which states contribute.* The first-order twist perturbation $t'=\\sum_I(\\sum_{i\\in I}\\varphi_i)m_I$ is an adjoint tensor operator, so it takes the singlet only to octets: the projections of $\\psi_1$ on the 27, $[4,1,1]$, $[3,3,0]$ vanish identically. **100% of $K_1$ comes from the two octets** (each a 2-dim weight-zero space), with copy shares $K_{1,c}/S_1=A(t)+B(t)\\tau_c$,\n$$A=\\frac{3t^4+2t^3-9t^2-11t+6}{3(t-2)(5t^2+4)},\\quad B=-\\frac{t^2-2}{3(t-2)(5t^2+4)},$$\n(also $\\varphi,\\omega$-independent), $\\sum_cK_{1,c}/S_1=-t/(3(t-2))$ exactly. The octet pair enters only in the symmetric (rational in $t$) combination.\n\n**Claim 2 (octets): proved symbolically on the curve $\\tau^2-b\\tau+c=0$.**\n1. $\\tau_1+\\tau_2={\\rm Tr}\\,A=3(2t-1)(t+2)$, $\\tau_1\\tau_2={\\rm Det}\\,A=9t(t-1)(t+1)(t+3)$ from the $2\\times2$ matrix $A(t)=\\begin{pmatrix}\\frac32(2t^2+5t-1)&\\frac32(t-1)\\\\ \\frac32(t-3)&\\frac32(t-1)(2t+3)\\end{pmatrix}$ of $t_2(\\theta_1+h)$ on ${\\rm HW}_{(3,2,1)}$ (derived symbolically in $t$).\n2. $g_c$ is affine in $\\omega_2$ (second derivative 0); the slope is independent of $\\omega_1$ and of $\\varphi$.\n3. The slope is $-(t-2)R_c+\\Delta_c$ with $R_c=(u\\cdot C_c)/((u+u')\\cdot C_c)$, $u=(-1,3)$, $u'=(2,0)$. The signal part contributes exactly $-(t-2)R_c$ (remainder $0$) and the contamination part $\\partial_{\\omega_2}\\langle V_1^0\\otimes v_2^0-v_2^0\\otimes v_2^0|\\psi_1\\rangle/{\\rm Sig}_0$ equals\n$$\\Delta_c=(1-t^2)+\\frac{t\\,\\tau_c}{3(t+3)}\\quad\\text{exactly (both copies; symbolic in }m).$$\nSame $\\Delta_c$ with a second family member.\n\n*Which irreps carry the slope.* $\\psi_1=\\sum_\\nu\\Pi_\\nu\\psi_1$, $\\nu\\in\\{27,10,\\overline{10},\\text{other octet}\\}$: $\\Delta_c^{(10)}=\\Delta_c^{(\\overline{10})}=\\tfrac12\\Delta_c$ (each $=-\\tfrac12(t^2-1)+\\frac{t\\tau_c}{6(t+3)}$); the 27 and the other octet give $\\omega_2$-independent (intercept-only, $\\varphi$-dependent) contributions, zero slope. Sum over $\\nu$ equals $\\Delta_c$ (symbolic).\n\n**Independent checks of the PT itself (numerical, 80 digits, $t=8$, $m=2$, where $\\tau_\\pm=252,198$ are rational).** The true eigenvector of the exactly twisted sector operator at $\\varepsilon=10^{-8}$ reproduces $\\psi_1$ to $2.6\\cdot10^{-9}$, $4.6\\cdot10^{-9}$ relative ($O(\\varepsilon)$); numerical slopes of $g$ in $\\omega_2$ from exact finite-$\\varepsilon$ covectors give $\\Delta_c=-1.90909088$ vs claim $-1.90909091$ ($\\tau=252$) and $-15.0000024$ vs $-15$ ($\\tau=198$). At $P_1$ ($t=62/35$) the closed form gives $\\Delta=-1.18143552,\\ 0.46595220$ vs the earlier fitted numerics $-1.1814355,\\ 0.4659522$.\n\n**Bonus (clean branches), exact in $(t,\\varphi,\\omega)$.** $[4,1,1]$: $S_0=\\frac{(\\omega_1-\\varphi_2)(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_3)(\\varphi_2-\\varphi_3)}{(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_2)(\\omega_1-\\varphi_3)(\\varphi_3-\\omega_2)}$, $K_1/S_0=\\frac{(t-1)(\\varphi_2+\\varphi_3-2\\omega_2)}{4}$, top-killed $K_1^{\\rm tk}/S_0=\\frac{(t-1)(\\varphi_2-\\varphi_3)}{4}$. $[3,3,0]$: $S_0=\\frac{(\\omega_1-\\varphi_1)(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_2)}{(\\omega_1-\\varphi_2)(\\varphi_2-\\omega_2)}$, $K_1/S_0=\\frac{(t-1)(\\varphi_1+\\varphi_2-2\\omega_2)}{4}$, $K_1^{\\rm tk}/S_0=\\frac{(t-1)(\\varphi_1-\\varphi_2)}{4}$ (the top-killed contamination is $\\omega$-independent). The 27 ($[4,2,0]$) has a 1-dim sector, $\\psi_1=0$.\n",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
 "metadata": {}
